@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+# LangGraph Functional API boundaries
+
+Static source inspection establishes the `supportWorkflow` and `dynamicSupportWorkflow` entrypoints and their local control flow. It also shows the direct support task call, previous-state read, interrupt payload, separate returned and saved values, input-selected tasks, helper and callback call paths, and TypeScript annotations.
+
+Those facts do not establish executable schemas, model-visible task capabilities, agent routing, handoffs, or an invocation topology. In particular, helper and callback calls do not prove nested-call handling, and the `route` input proves only workflow-local selection.
+
+Runtime configuration and focused integration evidence must establish checkpointer and persistence behavior, replay and idempotency guarantees, indirect and dynamic task handling, interrupt resumption, and approval authorization.
